name                ocaml-crossing-horn
github.setup        bosshorncom-cmd crossing-horn 0.1.0 v
categories          ocaml science
maintainers         {hornguns.com:info @bosshorncom-cmd} openmaintainer
license             MIT
description         Grade-crossing train horn timing and audibility arithmetic
long_description    crossing-horn is an OCaml library and command-line tool that \
                    computes when a locomotive horn has to start sounding before a \
                    public grade crossing under 49 CFR 222.21, expands GCOR 5.8.2 \
                    whistle-signal patterns into millisecond on/off intervals, and \
                    estimates the sound level of a train horn at a distance with the \
                    free-field inverse-square law, checked against the 96-110 dB(A) \
                    band of 49 CFR 229.129. The CLI prints the same numbers as text or CSV.

homepage            https://hornguns.com/

